 {r}←name CompareTwoFiles(filenames captions);parms
⍝ Compares two files with the comparison utility `name` as established by `EstablishComparisonTool`.\\
⍝ `filenames` must be two filenames, `captions` two character vectors; an empty caption leaves
⍝ the utility's own default in place.\\
⍝ Does not return before the user has closed a utility that allows editing, so the caller may
⍝ safely delete the two files afterwards.\\
⍝ Returns 0.
 parms←⎕SE.CompareFiles.ComparisonTools.⍎'CreateParmsFor',name
 parms.(file1 file2)←filenames
 :If 0<≢1⊃captions
     parms.caption1←1⊃captions
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢2⊃captions
     parms.caption2←2⊃captions
 :EndIf
 {}⎕SE.CompareFiles.Compare parms
 {}⎕DL 1.2×{0=⍵.⎕NC'edit1':0 ⋄ 0=⍵.(edit1+edit2)}parms ⍝ Avoid deletion/early deletion
 r←0
⍝Done
